    <div class="scrolly" id="stack">
      <div class="wrap scrolly-grid">
        <div class="sticky-pane">
          <canvas id="burgerCanvas" aria-hidden="true"></canvas>
          <div class="layer-tag" id="layerTag" aria-hidden="true"><b>01 / 06</b> &nbsp;TOP BUN · THE REBUILD</div>
        </div>
        <div class="chapters" id="chapters">

          <section class="chapter" data-layer="0">
            <span class="tag"><span class="swatch" style="background:#DD9A4E"></span><span class="t"><b>Layer 01</b> · Top bun · The rebuild</span></span>
            <h2>WLF Club</h2>
            <p class="lead">Growth &amp; Analytics Engineer at a healthcare clinic. <span>I found what the agency left live.</span></p>
            <p class="body">The $15,000 agency build was still serving dead $79.99 template membership pricing and 12 Lorem Ipsum pages, off the real offer by an order of magnitude, and perfectly readable to Google and to AI crawlers. I found it, then rebuilt wlfclub.com in-house: sitewide JSON-LD, FAQ schema, and an llms.txt so answer engines read the real business, a verify-gated deploy pipeline, and agency billing ended entirely. Migrated the clinic's DNS to Cloudflare with zero downtime and zero mail interruption, verifying 29 records and SPF/DKIM/DMARC under a strict reject policy before cutover.</p>
            <div class="stats">
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">$79.99</div><div class="l">dead template price still live</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">814 KB</div><div class="l">homepage weight, down from 2,027</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">0</div><div class="l">downtime, zero mail interruption</div></div>
            </div>
            <figure class="proof">
              <span class="shot"><img src="/proof/wlfclub.jpg" width="1280" height="800" alt="The live WLF Club homepage: Recover Smarter, Feel Better, Live Longer" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span>
              <figcaption><span>The business behind these numbers</span><a href="https://wlfclub.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">wlfclub.com →</a></figcaption>
            </figure>
          </section>

          <section class="chapter" data-layer="1">
            <span class="tag"><span class="swatch" style="background:#55833A"></span><span class="t"><b>Layer 02</b> · Lettuce · The free tier</span></span>
            <h2>Webspansion</h2>
            <p class="lead">A pro bono web studio I founded at 17. <span>19 live sites, all free.</span></p>
            <p class="body">Accessibility-first websites built free, as community service, for nonprofits, immigrant-owned local businesses, and community groups: intake, build, deploy, handoff, all solo. I also engineered the studio's own cookieless first-party analytics platform on Cloudflare Workers and D1, now tracking 27 client domains, and ran its growth with 23 SEO posts and 8 case studies.</p>
            <div class="stats">
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">19</div><div class="l">live sites shipped solo</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">27</div><div class="l">domains on my analytics platform</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">2023</div><div class="l">founded</div></div>
            </div>
            <figure class="proof">
              <span class="shot"><img src="/proof/webspansion.jpg" width="1280" height="800" alt="The live Webspansion homepage: I build free websites. Seriously. 19 free sites delivered" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span>
              <figcaption><span>Live, with public stats</span><a href="https://getwebspansion.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">getwebspansion.org →</a></figcaption>
            </figure>
          </section>

          <section class="chapter" data-layer="2">
            <span class="tag"><span class="swatch" style="background:#F2C14E"></span><span class="t"><b>Layer 03</b> · Cheese · The paid tier</span></span>
            <h2>Prospansion</h2>
            <p class="lead">The paid arm of Webspansion. <span>First build sold at $999.</span></p>
            <p class="body">Built Prospansion Studio, a multi-tenant Cloudflare Workers + D1 CMS giving paying clients self-serve site editing: invite-only signup, hashed tokens, single-use resets, and a fixed sanitizer-bypass XSS vulnerability, verified via exploit proof-of-fix. Deployed for nonprofit client Ocura. The first paid outside build closed at $999.</p>
            <div class="stats">
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">$999</div><div class="l">first paid build closed</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">Fixed</div><div class="l">sanitizer-bypass XSS</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">Ocura</div><div class="l">live nonprofit client</div></div>
            </div>
            <figure class="proof pair">
              <div class="pair-grid">
                <div class="pf">
                  <span class="pf-label">BEFORE</span>
                  <span class="shot"><img src="/proof/ocura-before.jpg" width="1280" height="800" alt="Ocura's old site: generic template hero with an oversized logo" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span>
                </div>
                <div class="pf">
                  <span class="pf-label after">AFTER</span>
                  <span class="shot"><img src="/proof/ocura-after.jpg" width="1280" height="800" alt="Ocura redesigned: editorial layout with the real student team photo, running on Prospansion Studio" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <figcaption><span>Same nonprofit, redesigned + moved onto the CMS, now on its own domain</span><a href="https://ocuraeyehealth.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ocuraeyehealth.org →</a></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <div class="links"><a href="https://prospansion.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">prospansion.com →</a></div>
          </section>

          <section class="chapter" data-layer="3">
            <span class="tag"><span class="swatch" style="background:#C79A5B"></span><span class="t"><b>Layer 04</b> · Patty · The data</span></span>
            <h2>Measurement, Attribution &amp; Warvis</h2>
            <p class="lead">The data layer. <span>Read 782 deals, found the real bottleneck.</span></p>
            <p class="body">I pulled two CSV exports out of the clinic's CRM and read all 782 sales opportunities. 95% had never reached a decision, but the ones that got worked closed at 92%. The problem was not lead volume, it was follow-up, and the growth plan changed from buying more ads to working the backlog. 62% of the wins had no recorded source at all, which is why I then instrumented the place from zero: GA4, Meta Pixel, Microsoft Clarity, and a first-party tracker doing identity resolution, stitching anonymous visitors to named CRM contacts so spend can be traced to real people. On top of that I built Warvis, the team's internal RAG assistant, now live for everyone: BM25 retrieval over 391 allowlisted notes, a weekly report pulling GoHighLevel, QuickBooks, and GA4 into one page, and an identity-resolution dashboard. Every system is architected PHI-free and out of HIPAA scope by design, and the one place AI touches member data runs through Vertex AI under a signed GCP business associate agreement, not a consumer API.</p>
            <p class="joke">Unrelated, but worth saying: the patty's grilled chicken, not beef. <b>I'm Hindu, so I swapped it.</b></p>
            <div class="stats">
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">782</div><div class="l">CRM deals analyzed by hand</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">92%</div><div class="l">win rate once a deal got worked</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">PHI-free</div><div class="l">by architecture, not by policy</div></div>
            </div>
            <div class="links"><a href="https://github.com/ashmitbohora" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="GitHub profile: Warvis">GitHub profile →</a></div>
          </section>

          <section class="chapter" data-layer="4" id="shipped">
            <span class="tag"><span class="swatch" style="background:#B93018"></span><span class="t"><b>Layer 05</b> · Special sauce · Shipped</span></span>
            <h2>Shipped Production Apps</h2>
            <p class="lead">Software that replaced something people were paying for. <span>And one model I trained myself.</span></p>
            <p class="body">The WLF members platform replaced Heads Up Health, a $12,000/yr vendor, with a build of my own: WHOOP and Apple Health sync, a 17-marker labs engine, role-scoped access, and a companion native app on TestFlight. Guruji (getguruji.com) is a free gamified app that teaches AI and coding to adult beginners, South Asian and immigrant families first, replacing $100/month paid tutoring for its first users: 196 lessons across 7 prerequisite-chained tracks, row-level-security auth, and WCAG AA type and tap targets because the learners are older. Auditing its own question bank is the thing I am proudest of: 57 of 58 newly written quiz items had the correct answer sitting in the same slot, so a learner could score 100% without reading a single lesson. I reshuffled the catalog and shipped a regression test that fails any track putting more than 55% of its answers in one position. Kiln is the other direction: a training loop that fine-tunes a 7B model on my own machine, with Claude as the teacher, to turn a scraped website into a structured redesign record. Held-out score went 0.84 to 0.99 in one round, and the keep-or-rollback gate later rejected a candidate that scored worse, which is the part that makes it safe to leave running.</p>
            <div class="stats">
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">$12,000/yr</div><div class="l">vendor software replaced</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">57 of 58</div><div class="l">biased quiz items I caught</div></div>
              <div class="stat"><div class="n">0.84&rarr;0.99</div><div class="l">Kiln held-out score, one round</div></div>
            </div>
            <figure class="proof">
              <span class="shot"><img src="/proof/guruji.jpg" width="1280" height="800" alt="Guruji live: a warm onboarding screen reading Your pocket guru, free, no login, 5 minutes a day" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></span>
              <figcaption><span>Guruji, live in production</span><a href="https://app.getguruji.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">app.getguruji.com →</a></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <div class="links">
              <a href="https://getguruji.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">getguruji.com →</a>
              <a href="https://app.bohoquest.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">app.bohoquest.app →</a>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section class="chapter" data-layer="5">
            <span class="tag"><span class="swatch" style="background:#DD9A4E"></span><span class="t"><b>Layer 06</b> · Bottom bun · The foundation</span></span>
            <h2>UT Austin: Statistics &amp; Data Science</h2>
            <p class="lead">The base that holds the whole stack up. <span>Class of 2029.</span></p>
            <p class="body">3.75 GPA. QuestBridge National College Match Finalist, 2024. $50,000 in merit scholarships: UT Impact Scholar ($48,000) and the Thomas &amp; Elizabeth Merner Scholarship in Natural Sciences ($2,000, 2026&ndash;2027). Coursework in probability and statistical inference, linear algebra, software design, and data science. Off campus I'm Director of Social for UT's Nepalese Student Association, where I lead a three-person team running a 17-event fall slate, campus partnerships, and ride logistics for everything off campus. Since 2021 I've co-led $10,000+ in fundraising and run logistics for health camps and blood drives. I'm a US permanent resident, so no sponsorship is needed. Sophomore now, looking for Summer 2027 internships in growth, analytics, and data science.</p>
            <div class="stats">
